  "text_input": "Patient was in his usual state since morning, then he started developing c/o shortness of breath, insidious in onset and gradually progressive in nature. Then he was taken to a local hospital where he was treated for the same and referred to KIMS Hospital for further evaluation and management.  Patient also had c/o cough with expectoration since 5 days which was insidious in onset and gradually progressive, with yellowish sputum, scanty in amount, non-foul smelling, mucoid in nature, which is non-blood stained. No diurnal variation or positional variation.  Also had c/o fever, low grade, intermittent type, associated with chills. He also has c/o burning micturition since 3 days, insidious in onset and gradually progressive. Patient also c/o tightness of chest. Initially he was able to walk about 100 m, but later on progressed to a point where he wasn’t able to walk even a few steps due to breathing difficulty. No H/o chest pain/ palpitation/ hemoptysis/orthopnea/decreased urine output.",
